==Kyrgyz==
{{wp|lang=ky}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ky|ur|پاکستان||Land of the Pure|tr=pākistān}}, from {{m|ur|پاک|t=pure, holy, immaculate, chaste, undefiled|tr=pak}} and {{der|ky|fa|ـستان|tr=-stân|t=[[-stan]]}}. The word was coined by {{w|Choudhary Rahmat Ali}}, who published it in the pamphlet ''Now or Never'' issued on January 28, 1933, as an acronym of the names of the "Muslim homelands" of western India—[[Punjab|'''P'''unjab]], [[Afghania|'''A'''fghania]], [[Kashmir|'''K'''ashmir]], [[Sindh|'''S'''indh]], and [[Balochistan|Balochis'''tan''']]. An '''i''' was later added to the name to ease pronunciation.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ky|[pakiˈstɑn]}}, southern: {{IPA|ky|[pækiˈstɑn]}}
{{rfap|ky}}

